/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/sessions/01KJ8MK2C4KQE66RNWZXW1TBT1/events.jsonl:{"ts":1771970489876,"seq":6818,"type":"prompt.sent","session_id":"01KJ8MK2C4KQE66RNWZXW1TBT1","data":{"iteration":6,"phase":"task-work","prompt":"# Kspec Automation Session - Task Work\n\n**Session ID:** `01KJ8MK2C4KQE66RNWZXW1TBT1`\n**Iteration:** 6 of 30\n**Mode:** Automated (no human in the loop)\n\n## Session Focus (applies to ALL iterations)\n\n> **Do your best, ensure code is high quality and you follow all ACs both main specs and attached traits. Be thorough. After submitting a PR run /codex PR and fix any issues it brings up. Ensure when spawning codex that you instruct it that it is running inside of a kspec ralph loop and in no uncertain terms should it blanket kill processes especially kspec or kspec ralph ones. Ensure the code you're writing is tested, reviewed and not only matches the letter of the tasks, specs, and AC but also the spirit. Do better, do more, be proactive and succeed!**\n\nKeep this focus in mind throughout your work. It takes priority over default task selection.\n\n\n## Current State\n```json\n{\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-02-24T22:01:29.852Z\",\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"context\": {\n    \"focus\": null,\n    \"threads\": [],\n    \"open_questions\": [],\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:05:45.847Z\"\n  },\n  \"active_tasks\": [],\n  \"pending_review_tasks\": [],\n  \"recent_notes\": [\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ74T8S\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Implement Session Start Dependency Display\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ8T16\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:49:07.005Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented 'unlocks N' annotation for session start output. Added computeUnlocksMap() that builds a reverse dependency map using ReferenceIndex — for each non-completed/cancelled task, resolves its depends_on refs and increments the count for the dependency target. Unresolvable refs are silently skipped per ac-unlocks-unresolvable. Added unlocks field to ReadyTaskSummary and BlockedTaskSummary types. Rendering shows green 'unlocks N' text when N>0, omitted when zero. 9 integration tests covering all 3 ACs: JSON + human output for ready/blocked tasks, zero omission, completed dependents excluded, and unresolvable ref handling via injected YAML with bogus ref.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ6KKSX\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Add multi-harness env injection\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ8RP3\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:25:35.658Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Added multi-harness env injection for Gemini CLI and OpenCode. Gemini CLI: writes to .gemini/.env in project root (auto-loaded by Gemini CLI). OpenCode: writes to project root .env (auto-loaded by Bun runtime). Both use a shared upsertDotenvSessionId() helper that replaces existing KSPEC_SESSION_ID lines or appends new ones. Updated performEnvInjection() routing to detect GEMINI_CLI=1 and OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR/OPENCODE_CONFIG env vars. Updated EnvInjectionResult method type. 8 new tests (3 Gemini, 3 OpenCode library, 2 CLI integration). Also updated existing CLI fallback tests to clear new env vars. All other harnesses (Cline, Aider, Copilot, Amp) fall through to the existing export fallback since they lack config-based env injection mechanisms.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ6KKS9\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Update setup with migration cleanup\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ8QWB\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:11:31.092Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"All 6 ACs (ac-setup-native, ac-no-task-limit-hook, ac-migrate-hooks, ac-idempotent, ac-worktree-guard, ac-worktree-allow) were already fully implemented and tested in the dependency task @implement-native-worktree-guard (PR #506). The setup.ts migration logic, native guard command installation, old script deletion, and idempotency handling are all in place with 7 tests in native-guard-setup.test.ts and 51 tests in guard-worktree.test.ts. This task is a no-op duplicate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ6KKRY\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Implement native worktree guard\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ8PVC\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T20:53:31.613Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Implemented native kspec guard worktree command. New file src/cli/commands/guard.ts with evaluateWorktreeGuard() function containing the same guard logic as the old bash script (dangerous pattern blocking, kspec-meta deletion prevention, cd/.kspec detection, split-quote bypass protection). Updated setup.ts to install 'kspec guard worktree' as PreToolUse hook instead of bash scripts, with migration logic that replaces old entries and deletes old script files. 51 new tests across 2 test files (guard-worktree.test.ts, native-guard-setup.test.ts). Updated 4 tests in enhanced-setup.test.ts to match native command behavior.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"active_todos\": [],\n  \"ready_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ8T2N\",\n      \"title\": \"Fix test failures when running inside ralph loop (env pollution)\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"testing\",\n        \"ralph\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ74T98\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Session Start Activity Timeline\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": \"@session-start-activity-timeline\",\n      \"tags\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ74T9Q\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Session Start Inbox Triage Awareness\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": \"@session-start-inbox-triage\",\n      \"tags\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ7CNF\",\n      \"title\": \"Audit and improve skills for agent self-sufficiency\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"skills\",\n        \"agent-quality\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocked_tasks\": [],\n  \"recently_completed\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ74T8S\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement Session Start Dependency Display\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T22:01:13.973Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #508. Added 'unlocks N' annotation to session start output for ready and blocked tasks. Counts only pending downstream dependents per spec. Unresolvable refs silently skipped. 11 integration tests covering all 3 ACs. Codex review finding (pending-only filter) addressed in fix commit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKSX\",\n      \"title\": \"Add multi-harness env injection\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:40:11.396Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #507. Added multi-harness env injection for Gemini CLI (.gemini/.env) and OpenCode (project root .env). Extracted shared upsertDotenvSessionId() helper. Updated performEnvInjection() routing. 8 new tests. All Codex review findings addressed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKS9\",\n      \"title\": \"Update setup with migration cleanup\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:11:44.250Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"All work was already completed in dependency task @implement-native-worktree-guard (PR #506). Setup.ts already installs native kspec guard worktree, migrates old bash script entries, deletes old script files, and handles idempotency. All 6 spec ACs have test coverage in native-guard-setup.test.ts. No additional code changes needed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKRY\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement native worktree guard\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T21:10:37.383Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #506. Native kspec guard worktree command replaces bash scripts. All 6 own ACs covered, all trait ACs annotated. Previous review findings addressed in fix commit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ752D\",\n      \"title\": \"Fix batch-exec-engine test timeout flakes\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T20:35:30.750Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #505. Three fixes: spawnSync 30s timeout, shadowPushAsync spawn+detached+unref pattern, vitest testTimeout 15s. All CI green.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKSK\",\n      \"title\": \"Simplify ralph with session budget\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T20:14:32.554Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #504. Replaced all marker file code with session budget APIs in ralph loop. 5 commits addressed all review findings across 4 review rounds. All CI checks passed. All 5 ACs covered with behavioral tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKRK\",\n      \"title\": \"Migrate end-loop to session state\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T17:16:03.481Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #503. Migrated end-loop signal from marker file to session state.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKR9\",\n      \"title\": \"Add session indicator to tasks ready\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:30:05.964Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Already fully implemented in @01KJ6KKQA (PR #499). Session indicator [session 01KJ...] shows in formatTask() and formatTaskListWithAutomation() in src/cli/output.ts. 13 integration tests in tests/session-scoped-task-claiming.test.ts cover all 6 ACs including ac-display. No new code needed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKQZ\",\n      \"title\": \"Add budget enforcement to task start\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T07:27:52.352Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged PR #501. Budget enforcement added to task start — checks session budget before allowing start, increments counter after successful transition, skips for resume/no-session/no-budget cases. 17 tests covering all 7 own ACs and 8 trait ACs (with N/A documented for non-applicable ones). All review threads resolved, CI green.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ6KKQM\",\n      \"title\": \"Implement session create command\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-24T06:54:59.114Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #500. Implements session create CLI command and createSessionWithBudget() library function with env injection for Claude Code, Codex CLI, and fallback. All 8 spec ACs covered, trait ACs tested. Fix commit addressed all 7 review findings.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recent_commits\": [\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"d69b34b\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"d69b34be23a94e6aaf0eab852ce30151377f7cf7\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T22:01:04.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"feat: add unlocks N dependency display to session start (#508)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"a503214\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"a503214754f535abeed2d3cd1cd48a786d5780f7\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T21:53:05.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: restrict unlocks count to pending dependents only\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"17661b0\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"17661b055231d115e3a9c97e74db20d66768c66d\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T21:49:22.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"feat: add unlocks N dependency display to session start\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"c2eb4f3\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"c2eb4f369f8e27d6b047a313fff0cd4b0cd01050\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T21:39:59.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"feat: add multi-harness env injection for Gemini CLI and OpenCode (#507)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"3c51c51\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"3c51c5191ceabfb839f5806070acd10005090e9c\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T21:31:00.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: address codex review findings for multi-harness env injection\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"4734c5d\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"4734c5daed01f264d77fd7dfaa9a68dad67742b3\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T21:25:49.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"feat: add multi-harness env injection for Gemini CLI and OpenCode\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"9674c85\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"9674c85ffb12f2aff35c294b4734ef562ac5b41a\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T21:10:30.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"feat: replace bash guard scripts with native kspec guard worktree command (#506)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"5076f9c\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"5076f9ca2c80aa53b36c6e035e62992c3f8d5d72\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T20:59:32.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: address codex review findings for native guard PR\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"902dbce\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"902dbce5e8b71e69070685ae4b39bdd2572bfc07\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T20:53:45.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"feat: replace bash guard scripts with native kspec guard worktree command\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"0c7b7ef\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"0c7b7ef3a2cfe7385fdead4ecc6fbd32146029c3\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T20:35:22.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: resolve batch-exec-engine test timeout flakes (#505)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"working_tree\": {\n    \"clean\": true,\n    \"staged\": [],\n    \"unstaged\": [],\n    \"untracked\": []\n  },\n  \"inbox_items\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFH76C\",\n      \"text\": \"Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search, validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs, (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage, (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover inbox.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T21:25:59.163Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"design\",\n        \"spec-model\",\n        \"meta\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFHJNZ\",\n      \"text\": \"Reverse spec lookup - kspec which <file> or kspec which <file:line> to find specs/ACs that reference or are implemented by a given code path. Useful for bug fixes to quickly discover what specs need updating. Could scan for // AC: annotations and spec_ref links. Instructive, helps find already-instrumented code.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T00:46:44.345Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"dx\",\n        \"tooling\",\n        \"reflection\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFPDCY\",\n      \"text\": \"Add cross-platform CI matrix testing - run core functionality tests on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Would catch issues like Unix-specific commands (which, cp -r) before they reach PR review. Consider: matrix strategy in GitHub Actions, platform-specific test skips where needed, focus on CLI commands and daemon lifecycle.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T21:50:37.263Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ci\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"dx\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFQ517\",\n      \"text\": \"E2E tests: Use isolated port range (not 3456) + cross-platform cleanup. Current approach conflicts with existing daemons. Should use high ephemeral port range and improve cleanup mechanism.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:43:39.058Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"e2e\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"reflection\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFYAHF\",\n      \"text\": \"E2E test dev mode - configure Playwright to work with vite dev server instead of requiring full build for faster test iteration (12+ seconds to 1-2 seconds)\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T23:34:35.746Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"e2e\",\n        \"dx\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGG6GY\",\n      \"text\": \"Improve derive granularity: Research suggests specs with 4+ ACs are candidates for splitting. Potential enhancements: (1) --by-ac flag to create tasks per AC group, (2) --max-acs N to auto-group, (3) implementation_phases field in specs, (4) derive templates for common patterns (cli-command, api-endpoint), (5) complexity warnings when specs are too large. See session research on task decomposition patterns from Linear, Atlassian, BDD/Example Mapping, and AI coding assistants.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-02T22:10:44.331Z\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGEMM\",\n      \"text\": \"Daemon debugging improvements: (1) Add --log-file or --verbose to 'kspec serve start', (2) Log resolved web UI path on startup, (3) Capture and show stderr when daemon fails to start within timeout. Consolidated from @01KFQ586, @01KFQ595, @01KFPH3D.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:32:32.926Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"daemon\",\n        \"dx\",\n        \"deferred\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGF4Y\",\n      \"text\": \"Project config file (kspec.config.yaml or .kspecrc): Configure shadow remote URL (enable separate repo for specs), feature toggles, default values (author, priority), validation strictness. Enables multi-repo projects sharing specs and tailoring kspec to project needs. Consolidated from @01KFGVVJ, @01KFGVVN.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:41:28.272Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"feature\",\n        \"config\",\n        \"dx\",\n        \"deferred\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGFB2\",\n      \"text\": \"AC test coverage analysis: 'kspec coverage @spec-ref' command to scan codebase for '// AC: @spec ac-N' annotations and report which ACs have test coverage vs gaps. Soft check for review, not blocking. Consolidated from @01KFHJNR, @01KFP9A6.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:44:48.658Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"cli\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"dx\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGG0K\",\n      \"text\": \"Shadow sync improvements: (1) Auto-resolve using rebase/merge-driver for cleaner sync, (2) Make sync warnings visible in CLI output (currently silent unless KSPEC_DEBUG=1), (3) Auto-detect common issues with suggested fixes. Consolidated from @01KFTDA7, @01KFHZR4.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:56:34.557Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"shadow\",\n        \"dx\",\n        \"cli\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stats\": {\n    \"total_tasks\": 641,\n    \"in_progress\": 0,\n    \"needs_work\": 0,\n    \"pending_review\": 0,\n    \"ready\": 27,\n    \"blocked\": 0,\n    \"completed\": 593,\n    \"inbox_items\": 90\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Instructions\n\nRun the task-work skill in loop mode:\n\n```\n/kspec:task-work loop\n```\n\nLoop mode means: no confirmations, auto-resolve decisions, automation-eligible tasks only.\n\n**Normal flow:** Work on a task, create a PR, then stop responding. Ralph continues automatically —\nit checks for remaining eligible tasks at the start of each iteration and exits the loop itself when none remain.\n\n**Do NOT call `end-loop` after completing a task.** Simply stop responding.\n`end-loop` is a rare escape hatch for when work is stalling across multiple iterations with no progress — not a normal exit path.\n","tasks":{"active":[],"ready":["01KJ8T2N","01KJ74T98","01KJ74T9Q","01KJ7CNF"]}}}
